{"availability":"available","full":"murtuzabuilds/outpost","name":"outpost","description":"A base of operations for AI agents: see the crew, set what each bot may touch, and decide the risky calls yourself. A 3D concept build.","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"JavaScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-02T17:39:01Z","updated":"2026-10-09T22:04:48Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://murtuzabuilds.github.io/outpost/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T22:06:06.665Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T22:06:06.665Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T22:06:06.665Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T22:06:06.665Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["The control room for the person who runs a company's AI agents.","Interactive demo · sample data · Case study · Umbra · Portfolio","Outpost is a concept product I designed and built. It is the control room for the person who runs a company's approved AI agents day to day. Each bot acts alone up to a limit it has earned, and anything risky waits at the Gate for a person's yes. It shows who on the crew is working and who is waiting, keeps a record of every decision, and lets you test a change to those limits on replayed shifts before it is applied."],"features":["They cannot see who needs them. In a table of logs a blocked agent looks the same as a busy one, and a blocked agent produces nothing.","Agents have no limits of authority. People do. A new hire cannot sign a $5,000 refund. In a 2026 Cloud Security Alliance survey, 53% of organisations said their agents had gone beyond their intended permissions (CSA,…","Approving everything does not scale. With enough agents, the person stops reading and starts clicking.","Nobody knows what a rule change will do until it is applied.","Kestrel Mutual is fictional."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/murtuzabuilds/outpost/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":